e restrict $\\theta $ to $[\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]$, we get the half-ellipse.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the half-ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2}].\n$$" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309935 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309936 13194139534783 true] [17592186309935 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309937 13194139534783 true] [17592186309935 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309938 13194139534783 true] [17592186309935 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309939 13194139534783 true] [17592186309935 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309940 13194139534783 true] [17592186309935 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534783 true] [17592186309935 1041 "selection" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309935 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309937 13194139534783 true] [17592186309935 1110 #uuid "626b8ca6-3e1b-53fb-936f-0f157d9bcf24" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309936 1034 "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309936 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534783 true] [17592186309936 1111 #uuid "3e038fbb-81b3-54e5-a08f-e7c5ad436372" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309937 1034 "\\theta \\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309937 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534783 true] [17592186309937 1111 #uuid "3ae3cd50-7070-5b4c-8d4f-1bf518c66e2c" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309938 1034 "\\theta \\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309938 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534783 true] [17592186309938 1111 #uuid "6a1aed6f-5ec6-5986-9447-1e1a0130c76f" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309939 1034 "\\theta \\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},2\\pi ]" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309939 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534783 true] [17592186309939 1111 #uuid "30781001-378a-57e0-a4db-b1f0febc4506" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309940 1034 "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309940 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534783 true] [17592186309940 1111 #uuid "f02bc288-4bae-5021-ad4e-5bd805fa119b" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309941 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309942 13194139534783 true] [17592186309941 1089 "q-106406" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309941 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534783 true] [17592186309941 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309941 1113 #uuid "4db2471c-43eb-5703-bc68-40fdaaff995e" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309941 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 2x & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 3y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 9{y}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=1.\n$$" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309942 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309943 13194139534783 true] [17592186309942 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309944 13194139534783 true] [17592186309942 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309945 13194139534783 true] [17592186309942 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309946 13194139534783 true] [17592186309942 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309947 13194139534783 true] [17592186309942 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534783 true] [17592186309942 1041 "selection" 13194139534783 