gin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=7$ and $b=4.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309949 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309950 13194139534783 true] [17592186309949 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309951 13194139534783 true] [17592186309949 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309952 13194139534783 true] [17592186309949 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309953 13194139534783 true] [17592186309949 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309954 13194139534783 true] [17592186309949 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534783 true] [17592186309949 1041 "selection" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309949 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309952 13194139534783 true] [17592186309949 1110 #uuid "3b85fdc8-4f51-5e10-b878-94c5a86d5e4d" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309950 1034 "x=49\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " 13194139534783 true] [17592186309950 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534783 true] [17592186309950 1111 #uuid "15b93a38-a2fe-5eac-a764-cb546f40d475" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309951 1034 "x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " 13194139534783 true] [17592186309951 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534783 true] [17592186309951 1111 #uuid "96bdb593-3805-57b7-8835-c1a8280cadf8" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309952 1034 "x=7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " 13194139534783 true] [17592186309952 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534783 true] [17592186309952 1111 #uuid "8036d244-dd2d-5c75-b51b-eb399c14d77a" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309953 1034 "x=\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " 13194139534783 true] [17592186309953 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534783 true] [17592186309953 1111 #uuid "b56a33bd-2395-5b52-a443-5f667669cc3a" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309954 1034 "x=16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=49\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " 13194139534783 true] [17592186309954 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534783 true] [17592186309954 1111 #uuid "e0737741-6eaa-5c11-950b-7ece83f087e4" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309955 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309956 13194139534783 true] [17592186309955 1089 "q-106715" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309955 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534783 true] [17592186309955 1100 "Determine the Cartesian equation of the ellipse\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309955 1113 #uuid "db659393-c5ee-5124-a2e0-8e5c4f1f44ed" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309955 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{x}{3} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{y}{5} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1.\n$$" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309956 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309957 131