cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{96}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50}=1.\n$$" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309968 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309969 13194139534783 true] [17592186309968 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534783 true] [17592186309968 1041 "field-1" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309968 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309969 13194139534783 true] [17592186309968 1110 #uuid "a68d4dad-6dbc-5905-9104-5cbbef20ce2a" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309969 1034 "\\frac{x^2}{96}+\\frac{y^2}{50}" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309969 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534783 true] [17592186309969 1111 #uuid "13dc05ed-4d2a-54f7-9143-1df7dfaf56b2" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309970 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309971 13194139534783 true] [17592186309970 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309973 13194139534783 true] [17592186309970 1089 "q-327835" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309970 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534783 true] [17592186309970 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/assets/6f983fda4328227558e46aaaec454db2ccc0611331495c923ad1d90c7cb3df8a.png)\n\nThe semi-ellipse above is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $\\theta ?$ Assume $\\theta $ is between $0$ and $2\\pi .$\n\n$\\theta \\in [${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$]$" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309970 1113 #uuid "72b22524-b982-564c-8317-a3f4cf8d743c" 13194139534783 true] [17592186309970 1145 "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=8$ and $b=3.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the *full* ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,